                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "37db395f-b416-444c-8e93-82240c991de2",
                                                "sense_id": "b97bbdd1-6261-3f8a-ae10-3e4898a5f81c",
                                                "text": "However the Labour Party and rail unions regard the move as a step closer to full nationalisation. TSSA General Secretary Manuel Cortes said: \"The ONS has candidly exposed the truth about our railways. They are now in public ownership. Grant Shapps must now take direct control of running them, rather than continue to line the pockets of privateers.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0a1b135d-a114-48b3-b799-ad2dafe3267d",
                                                "sense_id": "b97bbdd1-6261-3f8a-ae10-3e4898a5f81c",
                                                "text": "Despite criticisms which were made of the Railway Executive, it must be recalled that the general framework of the new railway set-up was established by statute, while this form of organisation was particularly well adapted for carrying out the unification of the railways—a very different thing from the purely political act of nationalisation, but an essential part of the objective of nationalisation."
                                            }
                                        ]
